// Pull request author: IsThisRitika
// Change: new rule
// Title: New Agent Skills Installation Attempt Via Node - Linux
// Sigma ID: ab582088-55d2-48f2-b707-ee5699d127cd
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Ritika <YOUR GITHUB HANDLE>
// Date: 2026-07-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.007
// Description: Detects the attempt to install new skills for AI agents using the "npx skills" command on Linux
//   systems. Agent skills enhance AI agents with new capabilities, but attackers may abuse this
//   mechanism to inject malicious commands executed by the agent on behalf of the user. The "npx
//   skills" command can install skills for various agents (e.g., Claude Code, Cursor, and others).
//   Analysts should review any installed skills to verify their legitimacy. Note: Tune this rule
//   based on whether AI agent tooling is allowed in your environment. In environments where such
//   tooling is authorized, this detection may reflect normal activity and the alert level should be
//   adjusted accordingly. In environments where AI agent tooling is not permitted, this activity is
//   likely suspicious and may require immediate investigation.
// False positives:
//   - This rule will be triggered when a new agent skill is installed regardless if it is benign or malicious.
//   - High false positive rate expected in environments where AI agent tooling is authorized and commonly used, such as developer workstations or CI/CD build agents.
// References:
//   - https://blog.lukaszolejnik.com/supply-chain-risk-of-agentic-ai-infecting-infrastructures-via-skill-worms/
//   - https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/blob/1f7fbc8d0e49c4e0601d364696bd1bdd15e80967/README.md
//   - https://opensourcemalware.com/blog/clawdbot-skills-ganked-your-crypto
//   - https://promptintel.novahunting.ai/molt
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/9f4385a83b710a218be47d7206b0a2b237f6d522/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_node_new_agent_skills_installed.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/node" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "npx-cli.js" and ProcessCommandLine contains "skills " and ProcessCommandLine contains " add ")
